From: davsar89 <17025345+davsar89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:24:21 +0100
Subject: fix(controller): remove the gyro zero-rate offset learned at rest

SDL's Switch driver reads the pad's factory zero-rate offset but never
subtracts it, so the game saw a constant rotation. A genuine Switch Pro
Controller lying on a table read +5.0, -0.9, -1.9 deg/s (noise 0.05 deg/s),
which made up/down motion drift while left/right was fine.

libs/gyroBias.h learns the offset whenever the pad lies still for a second
(gyro within 1 deg/s, smoothed gravity within 0.01 G) and Motion() removes
it from every reading. The first value learned is logged per controller.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/libs/controller.cpp |  15 +++++-
 src/libs/gyroBias.h     | 104 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 118 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 src/libs/gyroBias.h

diff --git a/src/libs/controller.cpp b/src/libs/controller.cpp
index 57d6f099..c24edd32 100644
--- a/src/libs/controller.cpp
+++ b/src/libs/controller.cpp
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include "kernel/pthread.h"
 #include "libs/dualSenseHaptics.h"
